# Test: a dns-resolver the reload removes leaves show system dns.
# Initial config: the observer plugin and service dns-resolver, whose written
#   forward list names configured with server 198.51.100.53.
# After SIGHUP: the observer plugin alone; the service block is gone, so the
#   engine removes the dns-resolver plugin while the daemon runs.
# Expected: show system dns lists the dns-resolver selection at
#   "service dns-resolver forward dns-source" before the reload, and after it
#   still answers the router's selection (consumer system) but no dns-resolver
#   consumer at all.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-home-cpe-23b review round 2 ISSUE 2: the dns-resolver's
#   OnBye handler (internal/plugins/dnsresolver/register.go,
#   followLearnedResolvers) sends its withdrawal while the engine removes the
#   plugin, inside the removal grace, and the registry forgets the consumer.
#   The unit test TestResolverWithdrawPublishesEmptySelection calls
#   withdraw() directly, so it proves neither the wiring nor that the emit
#   is read during removal.
# PREVENTS: a removed resolver whose last selection show system dns and
#   ze doctor keep reporting until the daemon restarts.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: with res.withdraw() taken out of the OnBye handler
#   (break overlay tmp/session/2026-11-07-104251/scratch/rwinv/
#   c23b-withdraw-on-bye/) the registry keeps a dns-resolver consumer, with
#   an empty selection list, after the reload removed the plugin, so the
#   post-reload poll never sees the consumer gone. Observed red
#   (rwinv/out-gb14/c23b-withdraw-on-bye.log:46): "the removed dns-resolver
#   is still listed with 0 selection(s)". The poll also requires the system
#   consumer's "system dns-source" selection, which proves the answer it
#   judged came from a live registry, not an empty one.
#
# Sequencing: the observer writes observer.initial-ok once the resolver is
#   listed; the trigger waits for it, copies config2.conf over ze-bgp.conf,
#   sends SIGHUP and writes reload.done, after which the observer polls for
#   the withdrawal. The reload therefore never races the first publication.
#
# No cmd= line carries `:timeout=`: a foreground command's timeout replaces
# option=timeout as the budget of the whole test.

option=timeout:value=60s

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external show-system-dns-withdraw-test {
		run "le test fixture plugin/show-system-dns-withdraw"
		encoder json
	}
}
service {
	dns-resolver {
		enabled true
		listener lan {
			ip 127.0.23.82
			port $PORT
		}
		allow-from 127.0.0.0/8
		forward {
			server 198.51.100.53 {
				port 53
			}
			dns-source {
				source configured
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
plugin {
	external show-system-dns-withdraw-test {
		run "le test fixture plugin/show-system-dns-withdraw"
		encoder json
	}
}
EOF_CONF2

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test fixture plugin/show-system-dns-withdraw-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: show system dns lists the dns-resolver's configured list before the reload
expect=stderr:contains=OK: show system dns drops the removed dns-resolver and keeps the router selection
reject=stderr:contains=reload error
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
